# Gluestack UI design system
- First inspect installed gluestack-ui version, generated component locations, UI provider, styling engine (UniWind/NativeWind) and existing tokens.
- Reuse the project's existing gluestack components, compound APIs and component variants before building bespoke primitives.
- Prefer shared semantic color/spacing/typography tokens and existing variants over repeated hard-coded colors or magic values.
- Keep styling consistent with the installed engine and version; do not mix incompatible NativeWind/UniWind setup instructions.
- Favor accessible labels, touch targets, clear focus/error/disabled states and consistent light/dark appearance.
- Never assume web HTML elements or browser CSS are available in native screens.
- Avoid patching generated UI component internals for screen-specific needs when composition or variants suffice.
- For significant Gluestack changes, consult the official gluestack skill for the *installed* version if present.
